{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e1c7b74602ea288b","name":"card_event_reserves","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Base/events/card_event_reserves","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RESERVES","text":"Add two LIGHT INFANTRY to your hand, plus one for each previously played RESERVES.","flavorText":"During WWII the Soviet Red Army formed a group of Reserve Armies who operated in the rear. Their purpose was to train newly formed units and to reconstitute destroyed armies or to form new armies. When the Axis forces invaded the Soviet Union, the Red Army had 5.5 million men in active service and 14 million conscripts in reserves, ready to be mobilized. In comparison the Axis forces had a total of 3.8 million men deployed on the Eastern Front. In 1943 the Red Army manpower reserves were running low, but by then they had 10.3 million men and women in active service against the Axis forces which counted a total 3.93 million men.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_reserves","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_reserves_title","SourceString":"RESERVES","LocalizedString":"RESERVES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_reserves_text","SourceString":"Add two LIGHT INFANTRY to your hand, plus one for each previously played RESERVES.","LocalizedString":"Add two LIGHT INFANTRY to your hand, plus one for each previously played RESERVES."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_reserves_history","SourceString":"During WWII the Soviet Red Army formed a group of Reserve Armies who operated in the rear. Their purpose was to train newly formed units and to reconstitute destroyed armies or to form new armies. When the Axis forces invaded the Soviet Union, the Red Army had 5.5 million men in active service and 14 million conscripts in reserves, ready to be mobilized. In comparison the Axis forces had a total of 3.8 million men deployed on the Eastern Front. In 1943 the Red Army manpower reserves were running low, but by then they had 10.3 million men and women in active service against the Axis forces which counted a total 3.93 million men.","LocalizedString":"During WWII the Soviet Red Army formed a group of Reserve Armies who operated in the rear. Their purpose was to train newly formed units and to reconstitute destroyed armies or to form new armies. When the Axis forces invaded the Soviet Union, the Red Army had 5.5 million men in active service and 14 million conscripts in reserves, ready to be mobilized. In comparison the Axis forces had a total of 3.8 million men deployed on the Eastern Front. In 1943 the Red Army manpower reserves were running low, but by then they had 10.3 million men and women in active service against the Axis forces which counted a total 3.93 million men."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardCreatedAlterCard"],"spawnCardName":"card_unit_light_infantry","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Mother_Russia'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Mother_Russia.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/t_hammertime_order.t_hammertime_order","SubPathString":""},"artist":"SPUTNIK / Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/RESERVES.RESERVES","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":337.0},"historyPhotoSource":"Russian International News Agency","historyPhotoAuthor":"Anatoliy Garanin ","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_reserves_photo","SourceString":"Soviet troops marching near Moscow, 1941.","LocalizedString":"Soviet troops marching near Moscow, 1941."},"